\section*{Abstract}
This white sheet defines the complete multi-node expansion pathway for integrating
new physical compute nodes into the OPTRON-STREAMS v1.0 and AstroElementa Engine v4.0
production mesh. It formalizes bare-metal validation, Kubernetes node registration,
GPUDirect RDMA virtual address isolation, and live telemetry synchronization required
to activate the closed-loop epoch engine across distributed GPU clusters.

\section{Node Addition Initialization Pathway}
The node expansion sequence follows a four-phase integration pipeline:

\begin{align*}
\text{Phase I} &\rightarrow \text{Bare-Metal Operating Parameters \& InfiniBand Validation} \\
\text{Phase II} &\rightarrow \text{Kubernetes Node Group Labeling \& Cluster Join Intercept} \\
\text{Phase III} &\rightarrow \text{GPUDirect RDMA Gateway Virtual Address Isolation} \\
\text{Phase IV} &\rightarrow \text{Telemetry Synchronization \& Epoch Loop Activation}
\end{align*}

\section{Phase I: Bare-Metal Operating Parameters}
Prior to joining the simulation mesh, the new node undergoes hardware-level screening.

\begin{itemize}
  \item Confirm EIA-310-E chassis compliance and vibration shielding.
  \item Ensure 48V DC bus-bar power delivery with $\pm 0.2\text{V}$ variance under load.
  \item Validate InfiniBand transceiver links using:
\end{itemize}

\begin{verbatim}
ibstat -v | grep -E "rate:|state:"
\end{verbatim}

Expected output: \textbf{Active} link state at \textbf{400 Gb/sec (NDR)}.

\section{Phase II: Kubernetes Node Group Labeling}
After network validation, the node is provisioned into the containerized cluster.

\subsection*{Cluster Join}
\begin{verbatim}
kubeadm join 10.128.0.100:6443 --token <secret-token> \
--discovery-token-ca-cert-hash sha256:<hash>
\end{verbatim}

\subsection*{Node Labeling}
\begin{verbatim}
kubectl label nodes node-04-alpha topology.kubernetes.io/zone=us-central-1a
kubectl label nodes node-04-alpha engine-tier=accelerator-hbm3
\end{verbatim}

\subsection*{Deployment Integration}
\begin{verbatim}
make deploy-milkyway
\end{verbatim}

\section{Phase III: GPUDirect RDMA Virtual Address Isolation}
The new node must establish host-free memory pathways for encrypted telemetry ingestion.

\subsection*{VRAM Region Allocation}
\begin{align*}
[0x7F000000 - 0x7F0FFFFF] &\rightarrow \text{Ingestion Region} \\
[0x7F100000 - 0x7F5FFFFF] &\rightarrow \text{Cyclotomic Registers} \\
[0x7F600000 - 0x7F9FFFFF] &\rightarrow \text{Fluid Simulation Grids} \\
[0x7FA00000 - 0x7FBFFFFF] &\rightarrow \text{Ledger Space}
\end{align*}

\subsection*{VRAM Locking}
\begin{verbatim}
optron-ctl --device-mask 0x00000008 --lock-vram-bounds 0x7F000000-0x7FBFFFFF
\end{verbatim}

\section{Phase IV: Telemetry Synchronization \& Epoch Activation}

\subsection*{RDMA Diagnostics}
\begin{verbatim}
optron-diag --test-rdma
\end{verbatim}

Ensures JWST, Gaia DR3, and LIGO telemetry interleave into 128-byte packed frames
with zero allocation lag.

\subsection*{Epoch Sync}
\begin{verbatim}
optron-ctl --sync-node-epoch --target-ip fe80::node04 --verify-mlkem
\end{verbatim}

